+// SSL_set1_reality_client enables experimental classic REALITY on a fresh
+// client connection. It copies a 32-byte X25519 server public key, a zero to
+// eight byte short ID, and a three byte client version. Configure supported
+// groups first: this selects a single X25519 key share, without changing the
+// advertised groups. Returns one on success and zero on invalid configuration.
+//
+// Authentication is mandatory, independent of verify mode and callbacks. No
+// WebPKI fallback is permitted. Only TCP/TLS 1.3 is supported; actual ECH, HRR,
+// sessions, early data, QUIC, DTLS and server mode fail closed. ECH GREASE is
+// allowed. All connection secrets remain internal to the handshake.
